<title>SOUTH AFRICA: RMB Holdings half yr shr jumps 67 pct.</title>
<headline>RMB Holdings half yr shr jumps 67 pct.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended December 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, headline (cts)   128	   vs   76.8</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     130.5	 vs   76.8</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		  33	   vs   23.5</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   95.8	  vs   56.4</p>
<p>    Income after tax	86.1	  vs   46.6</p>
<p>    Income from assoc.    37.0	  vs   25.6</p>
<p>Full name: Rand Merchant Bank Holdings</p>
<p>NOTE - Capitalisation shares would be awarded to shareholders registered on March 7, the terms of which would be announced separately.</p>
<p>The group said its latest results had been boosted by a 13.9 million rand turnaround from loss into profit by subsidiary Aegis Insurance.</p>
<p>The impact of this turnaround would be less significant for the next six months, although the board was confident that the group would be able to exceed its minimum targeted growth.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
